# BPB Website — design

## Direction

- Theme after **Backpack Battles** UI: cozy **parchment + leather** fantasy journal — see `docs/product/theme.md` and `assets/theme-refs/`
- Not a generic SaaS skin; not a pixel-clone of BPB Builds (same material family, closer to the real game + better UX)
- Preserve **tooltip** skin in `js/shared/tooltip.css` (cream/gold frames); page chrome stays parchment/leather

## Styling stack

- **Rely heavily on Tailwind** for page-specific layout and components
- Plain CSS is allowed for globals:
  - `css/theme.css` — how the site **looks** (tokens, atmosphere) ← start here
  - `css/shared.css` — optional shared layout helpers (not nav/footer markup)
- **Nav and footer** are JS modules: `js/shared/nav.js`, `js/shared/footer.js` — mounted from each page’s `index.js`
- Module CSS when needed (e.g. `js/shared/tooltip.css`, `js/shared/skeleton.css`)
- Do **not** put one-off page layout in giant shared CSS — use Tailwind on that page instead
- Do **not** re-implement the tooltip frame system in Tailwind utility soup
- Do **not** duplicate nav/footer HTML in every page by hand — use the shared JS modules
- Loading placeholders: shared parchment skeletons — see `.cursor/rules/skeleton.mdc` and `js/shared/skeleton.js`

## Theme cues (from game screenshots)

- Warm mottled parchment backgrounds; dark brown ink/frames
- Leather pouch cells for backpack grids
- Hanging fabric banners for strong CTAs (crimson / steel / forest)
- Rarity as colored paint-swipe labels
- Saturated item sprites as the colorful accent layer

## In-page forms & filter chrome (canonical)

Filter rails and in-page pickers (Item Library, builds filters, create Build info) use this parchment recipe.

**Form dialogs and onboarding** (event entry, stepped wizards, future form modules) use the rewards plate instead — see `.cursor/rules/forms.mdc`. Do not put those on Patch3.

**Reference surfaces**

| Surface | Where |
|---|---|
| Filter \| Build rail | `js/pages/create/rail-chrome.css` (`.cr-tabs`, `.cr-panel`, `.cr-label`, `.cr-input`, `.cr-submit`, `.cr-btn-quiet`, `.cr-modal`) |
| Patch3 shade bands | Filters, form fields, parked, essentials — `il-filter__shade` `::before` + `assets/icons/filters/Patch3.png` mask-border |
| OptionsFont labels | `.cr-label` / `.il-filter__check-label` — see `.cursor/rules/typography.mdc` |

**Form fields**

- Each control sits in a Patch3 shade band (`il-filter__shade cr-field-shade`)
- Field name: `.cr-label` (OptionsFont). Never Milonga on field labels or compact fact keys
- Helper copy: `.cr-hint` (Baskerville italic)
- Inputs: `.cr-input` / `.cr-textarea` (recessed ink well, Baskerville). Long notes use gold scrollbar (`.cr-textarea--notes`)
- Primary submit: `.cr-submit.is-ready` (green, Milonga sticker CTA)
- Secondary: `.cr-btn-quiet` (Baskerville, no sticker)
- Input dialogs that are filters or small pickers stay `.cr-modal` on parchment. Form dialogs and onboarding use the rewards plate (`.cursor/rules/forms.mdc`)
- Read-only session facts: Patch3 band + compact Baskerville `dl`, not a Milonga two-column dump and not a raw permalink

**Do**

- Recessed sections: Patch3 mask-border shade (`--build-shade` / `--il-shade` / warm ink wash), not a hard `border + border-radius` card
- Interactive outline/tint on the **shade** (`::before`), not a parchment cell rect
- Board-scoped confirms (sell, lock): stay over the relevant region; soft feathered / radial dim — no sharp full-bleed SaaS scrim
- Tokens: cream `#ffecdc` / `--il-cream`, ink `#3c261d` / `--il-ink`, gold `#eac914` / `--il-gold` for accents
- Gold scrollbars and grouping-style dropdowns when matching filter / History list chrome

**Don’t**

- Invent a second modal or form kit (no purple/gray dialogs, no SaaS input stacks)
- Stretch form dialogs toward full viewport width
- Put Milonga on filter checkboxes, field labels, or fact keys
- Hard-cut rectangular overlays that cover Parked / scrubber when only the bag needs attention
- Flat gray “bone” panels with a brown border pretending to be filter UI
- Default new controls to Inter / system pills / `rounded-full` chip clusters

## Typography & assets

Match the game’s face roles (detail in `docs/product/theme.md` + `.cursor/rules/typography.mdc`):

- **Libre Baskerville** (`--bpb-font-body`) — UI controls, filter labels (rarity / shop / crafted / gated), dropdowns, counts, body, meta
- **Milonga** (`--bpb-font-display`) — headings, nav banner words, tooltip item names, display / CTA stickers
- Filter / Options labels (`OptionsFont`): Baskerville **Regular** 26px, **3px** ink outline, cream fill, **no** letter-spacing tweak
- Do **not** default outlined filter/UI labels to Milonga; do **not** shrink shop rows vs rarity
- Avoid Inter/Roboto/Arial as the brand voice
- Fonts in repo (`assets/fonts/`); item sprites in Supabase Storage; theme refs in `assets/theme-refs/`

## Layout habits

- One job per section; reduce clutter
- Real game art as visual anchor when available
- Cards only when they aid interaction
- Desktop and mobile must both work

## Avoid

- Purple-on-white / purple-indigo “AI default” themes
- Flat gray pages with a brown border pretending to be parchment
- Copying BPB Builds’ web parchment 1:1
- Ignoring `docs/product/theme.md` / theme-refs once set
